                <paragraph>This also enables type conversion / parsing. E.g. Hydra can
                    only produce lists from the CLI, but this parsing layer can
                    convert them based on the annotated type. (Note: this only
                    works for pydantic v2 and higher.)</paragraph>
                <doctest_block classes="doctest" xml:space="preserve">&gt;&gt;&gt; def g(x: tuple): return x
&gt;&gt;&gt; conf = builds(g, x=[1, 2, 3])
&gt;&gt;&gt; instantiate(conf, _target_wrapper_=pydantic_parser)
(1, 2, 3)</doctest_block>
